Here are the limits of each function at $x=-3$, according to the graphs:

$\begin{align}
&\blueD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -3}h(x)=3}
\\\\
&\maroonD{\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -3}g(x)=2}
\end{align}$

Now we can find $\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -3}\Big(h(x)+g(x)\Big)$ using the fact that the limit of a sum of functions is the sum of the individual limits:

$\displaystyle\lim_{x\to -3}\Big(h(x)+g(x)\Big)=\lim_{x\to -3}h(x)+\lim_{x\to -3}g(x)$
